Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `gsod2023.stn` / `gsod2023.wban`: join key to match a station’s daily observation with its master‑record.  
• `stations.usaf` / `stations.wban`: join key that identifies the same station in the stations table.  
• `stations.country`: ISO–style two‑letter country code; allows us to keep only “US” and “UK/GB”.  
• `gsod2023.date`: filter to the month of October 2023 and aggregate “per‑day”.  
• `gsod2023.max`, `gsod2023.min`, `gsod2023.temp`: daily maximum, minimum and mean temperature; required for the three “difference” metrics.  
• Exclusion rules: any of those three fields equal to their missing flags (`9999.9` for max/min/temp) must be removed from all calculations.

Typical filter block  
```
WHERE g.date BETWEEN '2023-10-01' AND '2023-10-31'
  AND g.max <> 9999.9
  AND g.min <> 9999.9
  AND g.temp <> 9999.9
  AND s.country IN ('US','UK','GB')
```

